# standards source registry: <local filename> <TAB> <absolute source path> <TAB> [fork]
# Copy to .sources and fill in. Read by sync.sh, gitignored because it holds
# absolute paths and the names of the repos that own each file.
#
# Two kinds of entry:
#   copy  (default)  the local file tracks its source exactly; any difference is
#                    drift and --pull is the fix.
#   fork             the local file carries sections we wrote on top of the
#                    source. sync.sh reports it and REFUSES to --pull over it.
#                    Use --diff to see what moved upstream and merge by hand.
#
# design-principles.md	/absolute/path/to/your-project/docs/design-principles.md
# social-app-principles.md	/absolute/path/to/your-project/docs/social-app.md	fork
#
# A standard with no upstream owner needs no line here at all.
